vedis
------------------------------------------
Vedis is an embeddable datastore C library built with over 70 commands similar
in concept to Redis but without the networking layer since Vedis run in the
same process of the host application.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libvedis-devel-1.2.6-1bl3
  libvedis0-1.2.6-1bl3
  pkg-config-3.0.11-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.13-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://vedis.symisc.net/

Canonical download:
  https://vedis.symisc.net/db/vedis-ds-126.zip

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack vedis-1.2.6-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./vedis-1.2.6-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/vedis-1.2.6-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/vedis-1.2.6-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libvedis0-1.2.6-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libvedis-devel-1.2.6-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(vedis)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/vedis.README
  /usr/share/doc/vedis/license.txt

(libvedis0)
  /usr/bin/cygvedis-0.dll

(libvedis-devel)
  /usr/include/vedis.h
  /usr/lib/libvedis.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/vedis.pc

------------------

Port Notes:

